---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro';
const plans = [
 { weeks: '4 weeks', name: 'Find your baseline', href: '/4-week-program/', fit: 'New to hanging or returning after time away.', job: 'Learn a controlled setup, repeat a manageable session and keep a simple record.' },
 { weeks: '8 weeks', name: 'Make practice consistent', href: '/8-week-program/', fit: 'You already have a repeatable, comfortable hold.', job: 'Use two four-week blocks to compare sessions and change one variable at a time.' },
 { weeks: '12 weeks', name: 'Review a longer training block', href: '/12-week-program/', fit: 'You want a longer record alongside your existing training.', job: 'Plan three review points. Keep the same assistance category so the record stays useful.' },
];
---
<Article title="Dead Hang Training Programs: 4-Week, 8-Week & 12-Week Plans" description="Choose a free 4, 8 or 12-week dead hang planning framework. Set manageable intervals, keep a training log and print a session planner without signing up.">
<div class="article-header"><div class="article-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span>Training plans</div><h1 class="article-h1">Dead hang training plans.</h1><p class="article-subtitle">Choose a planning window. Set holds you can control. Review what you actually did. These free frameworks organise practice; they do not promise a particular hold time.</p></div>
<div class="article-body">
<h2>Choose your starting point</h2><p>Use your experience and comfort with the movement, not a claimed population rank. A supported hold is a legitimate starting variation. Stop if you have pain and seek suitable advice before training through an injury.</p>
{plans.map(plan=><section class="plan-option"><p class="dh-eyebrow">{plan.weeks}</p><h3>{plan.name}</h3><p><strong>{plan.fit}</strong> {plan.job}</p><a class="text-link" href={plan.href}>Read the {plan.weeks.replace(' ', '-')} framework →</a></section>)}
<h2>Set a session you can control</h2><p>The workspace starts with 30 seconds of hanging, 60 seconds of rest and three sets. These are editable timer settings, not a prescription. Shorten the hold, add assistance or use a different rest interval to match your actual ability.</p><p>Save a personal goal if you want it on this device. Record actual holds after training. Avoid treating a timer reaching zero as proof that you completed a set.</p><a class="dh-btn" href="/training-log/">Set up my goal, timer & log</a>
<h2>Fit hanging into your wider activity</h2><p>Dead hangs are one movement. They do not replace a balanced strength and aerobic programme. NHS guidance recommends strengthening the major muscle groups on at least two days each week; it does not prescribe a dead-hang routine.</p><p><a href="https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/exercise/physical-activity-guidelines-for-adults-aged-19-to-64/">Read the NHS adult activity guidance</a>, including advice for returning to exercise or exercising with a medical condition.</p>
<section id="print-plan" class="print-planner"><p class="dh-eyebrow">DeadHangs.com / session planner</p><h2>Take your plan to the bar.</h2><p>Write the settings before your session. Fill in actual results afterwards. Keep assisted and unassisted holds separate.</p><div class="planner-lines"><p>Date:</p><p>Bar / grip / assistance:</p><p>Planned hang seconds / rest seconds / sets:</p><p>Actual holds:</p><p>What to repeat or change next time:</p></div><p class="small-copy">Stop if painful. Step down under control. This is a personal record, not a health assessment.</p><button type="button" class="dh-btn print-button">Print blank planner</button></section>
<h2>Equipment comes after the setup</h2><p>Check the bar's instructions, mounting requirements, clearance and load rating. A suitable bar matters more than a longer shopping list. The <a href="/equipment-guide/">equipment guide</a> compares mounting options and discloses affiliate links.</p>
</div></Article>
<script>document.querySelector('.print-button')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());</script>
